></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Li, P., G. McDermott, and R.K. Strong. <year>2002</year>. Crystal structures of RAE-1beta and its complex with the activating immunoreceptor NKG2D. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;86.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11825567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">McFarland, B.J., and R.K. Strong. <year>2003</year>. Thermodynamic analysis of degenerate recognition by the NKG2D immunoreceptor: not induced fit but rigid adaptation. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>803</fpage>&#x02013;812.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14670298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">McFarland, B.J., T. Kortemme, S.F. Yu, D. Baker, and R.K. Strong. <year>2003</year>. Symmetry recognizing asymmetry: analysis of the interactions between the C-type lectin-like immunoreceptor NKG2D and MHC class I-like ligands. <source>Structure.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>411</fpage>&#x02013;422.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12679019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Radaev, S., B. Rostro, A.G. Brooks, M. Colonna, and P.D. Sun. <year>2001</year>. Conformational plasticity revealed by the cocrystal structure of NKG2D and its class I MHC-like ligand ULBP3. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>1039</fpage>&#x02013;1049.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11754823</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wolan, D.W., L. Teyton, M.G. Rudolph, B. Villmow, S. Bauer, D.H. Busch, and I.A. Wilson. <year>2001</year>. Crystal structure of the murine NK cell-activating receptor NKG2D at 1.95 A. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>248</fpage>&#x02013;254.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11224525</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Borrego, F., M. Ulbrecht, E.H. Weiss, J.E. Coligan, and A.G. Brooks. <year>1998</year>. Recognition of human histocompatibility leukocyte antigen (HLA)-E complexed with HLA class I signal sequence-derived peptides by CD94/NKG2 confers protection from natural killer cell&#x02013;mediated lysis. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>187</volume>:<fpage>813</fpage>&#x02013;818.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9480992</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Braud, V.M., D.S. Allan, C.A. O'Callaghan, K. Soderstrom, A. D'Andrea, G.S. Ogg, S. Lazetic, N.T. Young, J.I. Bell, J.H. Phillips, et al. <year>1998</year>. HLA-E binds to natural killer cell receptors CD94/NKG2A, B and C. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>391</volume>:<fpage>795</fpage>&#x02013;799.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9486650</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brooks, A.G., F. Borrego, P.E. Posch, A. Patamawenu, C.J. Scorzelli, M. Ulbrecht, E.H. Weiss, and J.E. Coligan. <year>1999</year>. Specific recognition of HLA-E, but not classical, HLA class I molecules by soluble CD94/NKG2A and NK cells. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>162</volume>:<fpage>305</fpage>&#x02013;313.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9886400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lee, N., M. Llano, M. Carretero, A. Ishitani, F. Navarro, M. Lopez-Botet, and D.E. Geraghty. <year>1998</year>. HLA-E is a major ligand for the natural killer inhibitory receptor CD94/NKG2A. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>95</volume>:<fpage>5199</fpage>&#x02013;5204.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9560253</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brostjan, C., T. Bellon, Y. Sobanov, M. Lopez-Botet, and E. Hofer. <year>2002</year>. Differential expression of inhibitory and activating CD94/NKG2 receptors on NK cell clones.